(in-ns 'go.arbace.pyctypes) ^{:go/comments [[3 1 "// The limited C API's remainder (queue 268; doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, \"As built: 268\"): the functions of queue 262's"] [4 1 "// list of natives not provided (`.tmp/q262/missing.txt`) that the world's _testlimitedcapi reaches and pyi's objects"] [5 1 "// answer directly: dicts, sets, lists, tuples, ints, floats, complex numbers, bytes, bytearrays, the number, mapping"] [6 1 "// and sequence protocols, str's core, weak references, imports' module table, PyMem. Each follows its CPython 3.14.10"] [7 1 "// definition (Objects/dictobject.c, setobject.c, listobject.c, tupleobject.c, longobject.c, floatobject.c,"] [8 1 "// complexobject.c, bytesobject.c, bytearrayobject.c, abstract.c, unicodeobject.c, weakrefobject.c, Python/import.c,"] [9 1 "// Objects/obmalloc.c): the type checks and their messages, the operation through pyi's own (its type's method or"] [10 1 "// protocol, as CPython's calls the type's slot). The PSF's license (LICENSE.md)."] [21 1 "// callMeth calls o's method name with args."] [30 1 "// each calls f on each item of iter(o) until it returns an error (Iterate's)."] [38 1 "// callBuiltin calls builtins.name with args."] [47 1 "// opArgs are a native's object arguments, nil for NULL; err when one is NULL (null_error)."] [67 1 "// bigOf is o as an int (its __index__), CPython's _PyNumber_Index."] [79 1 "// asUnsigned is PyLong_AsUnsignedLong's family: o an int (no __index__), in [0, 2**bits)."] [98 1 "// asSignedBits is PyLong_AsInt32's family: o's __index__ in the signed range of bits."] [110 1 "// unsignedIndex is PyLong_AsUInt32's family: o's __index__ in [0, 2**bits)."] [127 1 "// storeInt writes the int v of size bytes at p (an output argument), when p is not NULL."] [144 2 "// ---- dicts (Objects/dictobject.c) ----"] [185 34 "// _PyErr_SetKeyError"] [209 2 "// PyDict_GetItem and GetItemString: borrowed, errors suppressed"] [313 2 "// PyDict_Next(d, Py_ssize_t *pos, PyObject **key, PyObject **value): borrowed references"] [358 2 "// ---- sets (Objects/setobject.c) ----"] [384 3 "// set_contains_key: the key hashed as is (set's `in` retries an unhashable set as a frozenset; PySet_Contains not)"] [410 4 "// a brand new frozenset (C holds its only reference: PyFrozenSet_New's) is filled in place"] [418 4 "// _PyErr_BadInternalCall(__FILE__, __LINE__) of Objects/setobject.c's PySet_Add (a frozenset too: pyi's are"] [419 4 "// never brand new to C)"] [446 2 "// ---- lists and tuples (Objects/listobject.c, tupleobject.c) ----"] [544 2 "// ---- ints (Objects/longobject.c) ----"] [592 2 "// longobject.c's messages, as they are"] [635 2 "// PyLong_AsInt32 (o, int32_t *out) and the family: 0, or -1 with an error"] [640 24 "// *value left as it was"] [656 2 "// ---- floats and complex numbers ----"] [662 3 "// a str or a buffer only (Objects/floatobject.c; queue 270): float() also takes numbers"] [681 3 "// a new sys.float_info (floatobject.c's PyFloat_GetInfo makes one each call)"] [712 2 "// ---- the number protocol (Objects/abstract.c) ----"] [742 2 "// ---- the mapping and sequence protocols ----"] [956 2 "// ---- bytes and bytearrays (Objects/bytesobject.c, bytearrayobject.c) ----"] [993 47 "// the mirror's ob_sval (queue 269)"] [1106 2 "// ---- str's core (Objects/unicodeobject.c) ----"] [1421 3 "// PyUnicode_DecodeXXX(const char *s, Py_ssize_t size, const char *errors)"] [1469 2 "// ---- weak references (Objects/weakrefobject.c) ----"] [1493 2 "// ---- the module table (Python/import.c) ----"] [1522 2 "// PYC_MAGIC_NUMBER_TOKEN (Include/internal/pycore_magic_number.h: 3627, CPython 3.14's) as import.c gives it"] [1596 31 "// borrowed: sys.modules holds it"] [1609 2 "// ---- types (Objects/typeobject.c): every pyi type is ready; the cache is pyi's own"] [1614 3 "// a type object of C's memory (queue 269): a static PyTypeObject, or one C filled after type's tp_alloc"] [1621 2 "// ---- the codecs' stateful decoders (Objects/unicodeobject.c over _codecs' functions)"] [1623 3 "// PyUnicode_DecodeUTF16(s, size, errors, int *byteorder) and its Stateful (..., Py_ssize_t *consumed)"] [1668 3 "// PyUnicode_DecodeUTF8Stateful(s, size, errors, Py_ssize_t *consumed)"] [1701 2 "// PyUnicode_Translate is _PyUnicode_TranslateCharmap: a code point the mapping lacks (LookupError) is kept, one it"] [1702 2 "// maps to None is undefined, given to the errors handler (str.translate deletes it)"] [1718 2 "// ---- files (Objects/fileobject.c) ----"] [1763 22 "// Py_PRINT_RAW"] [1834 2 "// ---- memory (Objects/obmalloc.c) ----"] [1844 2 "// the inline accessors of the old limited versions, functions since 3.14's (Include/object.h)"] [1859 1 "// appendStr is PyUnicode_Append (PyObject **pleft, PyObject *right) and AppendAndDel."] [1892 1 "// cmpRunes is PyUnicode_Compare's order: by code point."] [1912 1 "// builtinMethod is a built-in type's method by name (list.sort)."] [1918 1 "// getargsKeywords is PyArg_ParseTupleAndKeywords (Python/getargs.c, vgetargskeywords): the positional arguments and the"] [1919 1 "// keywords of kwargs (nil: none) converted by format into the pointers, the parameters named by kwlist (a char *[] in"] [1920 1 "// the world, NULL-terminated; empty names are positional-only)."] [2035 63 "// skipitem leaves the format at the unit"] [2072 4 "// new_kwtuple: the keyword-capable names decoded strictly (an invalid one is its UnicodeDecodeError)"] [2081 27 "// (without _Py_CalculateSuggestions' \"Did you mean\")"] [2089 3 "// every extra keyword matched a name (a str subclass whose hash is not its text's: queue 270)"] [2099 1 "// parseKeywords is PyArg_ParseTupleAndKeywords's native."] [2122 1 "// addModule is PyImport_AddModuleRef: sys.modules[name], a new module put there when absent."] [2152 1 "// translateCharmap is unicodeobject.c's _PyUnicode_TranslateCharmap over pyi's str."] [2186 3 "// the run of undefined characters goes to the handler"]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[50 12] [50 19] [153 35] [186 51]